02:20:09,600 --> 02:20:15,600
Most of the film was personally financed by media mogul Ted Turner.

17
02:28:55,200 --> 02:29:01,200
Originally running over five hours in length, the film was cut by an hour and a half for its 2003 theatrical
release, with the full "Extended Director's Cut" being released eight years later in 2011.

18
02:37:40,800 --> 02:37:46,800
The film was both a critical and commercial failure.

19
02:46:26,399 --> 02:46:32,399
Although film critics complimented its performances and historically accurate details
such as costumes, they criticized its length, pacing, and screenplay.

20
02:55:12,000 --> 02:55:18,000
The film was also heavily criticized by both critics and
historians for its "pro-Confederate slant".

21
03:03:57,600 --> 03:04:03,600
The Southern Poverty Law Center, as well as numerous writers and historians,
pointed out that the film endorsed the "Lost Cause" myth.

22
03:12:43,200 --> 03:12:49,200
Both Shaara and Maxwell expressed displeasure at the theatrical edition of the film, and its poor returns forced
Turner to cancel Maxwell's planned adaptation of Shaara's final Civil War novel The Last Full Measure.

23
